    <main class="lesson-container py-4">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <div id="tutorial-header"></div>
        
        <div class="content lesson-content" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <p>Ping is a network utility used to test the reachability of a host on an IP network. It sends ICMP Echo Request packets and waits for an Echo Reply.</p><h3>How to Use It</h3><p>Open your command line and type <code>ping google.com</code>. If you get replies, you have internet connectivity. If you get <code>Request timed out</code>, the packet was lost or blocked by a firewall.</p><h3>Related Command</h3><p>Learn more about <a href='../../commands.html' class='cmd-badge' style='display:inline-block'>ping</a> in our Commands section.</p>
        </div>
        
